fixNotes.d1116-budget-all:
Your area builds A task's budget counts everything spent on it (its work, the critic's reviews and the fixes after a review) as one figure. Its runs and its reviews stop at that figure. A work run keeps room for its review when the budget can hold it. A review that does not fit pauses cleanly with the work kept, and one Continue gives it what it needs. The estimate includes the review, the plan card equals the Start dialog, and the screens and the session review set one figure against the budget and the estimate (the owner's answer of 2026-11-16, which replaces run L3's work-only default). Its size and cut line: large: 13 items (BA-1 to BA-13), one fixer, one long run, a little more than d1109-oversize-pause.
- The larger items are BA-1, BA-3, BA-4, BA-6 and BA-7: engine logic with a composed case each, and BA-3 and BA-7 with restart cases.
- BA-2, BA-5, BA-8 and BA-9 are medium.
- BA-10 to BA-13 are one function, one test or one doc each.

Cut line, may end in not_done with the evidence:
- BA-9's drawer header and the New task / Edit hints;
- BA-12, the Start dialog's warning (carried to the leftovers with its wording);
- BA-7's refresh before the start check and the plan card (the fold at the next restart still takes those tasks; the live hook at the close is not cut).

Never in not_done:
- BA-1: every review call on the task, the figure equal to the ledger's;
- BA-2: old tasks counted the same way;
- BA-3: the review capped at the task's left on the full total, its refusal named the task's budget, the clean pause with the work kept, the review-only pass after Continue, the refused estimate on the card, and its restart case;
- BA-4: each work run and fix keeps R + W when the budget holds it, the run's cap source from its own cap; no budget, wrap-up line, monthly cap or plan-share cap is ever passed;
- BA-5: one Continue lets a waiting review run (the two-call case);
- BA-6: the estimate includes the reviews and fixes, with the plan card equal to the Start dialog;
- BA-7: one sample per task, live equals the fold after a restart, the close-twice cases included;
- BA-8: the planned tasks' figure against the estimate, with old rows read as written;
- BA-9's TaskCap words, tooltip and the one figure on the row and on Costs;
- BA-10: the fake daemon in step with the real one.
